window.products.push({"id":108804,"name":"Idler Pulley Wpw10547292 W10547292 Whirlpool Dryer Replacement Medb400vq0 Mgdb880bw0 Wed8000bw0 Wed8500bw0 Wed8600yw0 Medb200vq0 Medb750yw0 Medb850yg0","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":9.95,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61ojaMjqwqS._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"💡 Idler Pulley WPW10547292 W10547292 - A high-quality exact equivalent for part numbers AP6022817, 2683183, 8547160, PS11756154, WPW10547292VP. Wpw10547292 Idler Pulley is compatible with Kenmore, Maytag, Whirlpool dryer. It fits hundreds of models and can be installed in a few minutes. W10547292 Dryer Idler Pulley is a vital component of a dryer's belt tensioning system, and should be inspected regularly to ensure proper function and prevent premature belt wear or other issues. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace Whirlpool Wpw10547292? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. Whirlpool W10547292 Idler Pulley will help if your appliance is noisy, and doesn't tumble or start. W10547292 Whirlpool Dryer Idler Pulley Replacement helps the belt to rotate the drum. 💡 The Maytag Wpw10547292 is responsible for maintaining tension on the dryer belt, which helps keep the drum rotating during the drying cycle. Maytag Dryer Idler Pulley Wpw10547292 consists of a plastic wheel with a bearing in the center and a bracket that holds the wheel in place. Dryer Idler Pulley Wpw10547292 meets or exceeds all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 How do I know if my dryer idler pulley is bad? If you suspect that your Idler Pulley is faulty, there are a few steps you can take to diagnose the issue. First, visually inspect the pulley wheel and bracket for any signs of wear or damage. You may also notice unusual noises or vibrations during the drying cycle, which could be a sign of a bad idler pulley. Additionally, you can try manually turning the pulley wheel to see if it moves smoothly or if there is any resistance or grinding. 💡 Is dryer idler pulley supposed to spin? Yes, the Idler Pulley in a dryer is supposed to spin freely. It's important for the Pulley to spin smoothly to reduce friction on the dryer belt, which helps prevent the belt from wearing out prematurely. If the Idler Pulley doesn't spin freely or if you notice any unusual noises or vibrations, this could be a sign that the Pulley is damaged or has worn out bearings. To avoid the harm to the dryer's components, it's better to replace the Idler Pulley.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61ojaMjqwqS._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B07L14TRF4","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-108804","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07L14TRF4","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B07L14TRF4","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
